{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3151","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3151","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3151\",\"parent_revision\":\"dbfe8d9f5494093200f199bcc02bfc2b825973ed\",\"root_revision\":\"89f26996ef841cb0b9435434f28831a0f5e6b4d587248b0a9e8fed8ea5a979d8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA SAM task is not a file. It is an entry in the configured backend, read and written programmatically through the MCP operations or the CLI, addressed as `P{id}/T{id}`. It is never read or written by a file operation.\\n\\nThe plugin's own content still says otherwise in 138 places \u2014 92 in markdown, 46 in Python under `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/`. This has been corrected by instruction repeatedly over roughly six months and has not closed.\\n\\nObserved cause: correcting the prose does not work, because two authoritative sources actively regenerate it.\\n\\nFirst, the language is a live data contract, not a wording choice. `/dh:start-task` writes a session context file whose JSON key is literally `task_file_path` and whose value is a real filesystem path. The test suite exercises it across four files:\\n\\n    {\\\"task_file_path\\\": \\\"plan/P001.yaml\\\", \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"T1\\\"}\\n    {\\\"task_file_path\\\": \\\"/tmp/plan/P001-feature.yaml\\\", \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"T1\\\", ...}\\n\\nAny agent or hook reading that payload is correct to call the thing a task file \u2014 that is what the field is named and what it holds. A partial migration also stalled here: `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` asserts `\\\"task_file_path\\\" not in source` for one module while the key remains the contract everywhere else, which pins the inconsistency rather than closing it.\\n\\nSecond, `AGENTS.md` instructs every agent to go and learn the file-based model. Its \\\"Required Reading by Task Type\\\" section routes task work to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 29K, referenced from ten documents, with a second copy at `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`.\\n\\nSo the loop is: an agent reads `AGENTS.md`, is told to load `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, learns tasks are files, and writes that into whatever it edits \u2014 in good faith, and consistently with the live JSON key. Prose is the loop's output, so each prose-scoped correction fixes the open file and leaves the sources intact.\\n\\nImpact: agents are taught a storage model the system does not use. Concrete consequences already observed \u2014 `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` documents a parameter named `task_file_path`; `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines the `plan` field as \\\"relative path to SAM task file\\\"; `skills/execution/SKILL.md` has a workflow step \\\"Read Task File\\\"; `agents/code-reviewer.md` says \\\"Read the SAM task file using `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\\\", calling the right operation by the wrong name. A path-based handoff also silently produces an empty read in a worktree-isolated dispatch rather than an error, and on a remote backend there is no file to read at all.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the ordering that would close it appears to be structural-first \u2014 rename the context-file key and its payload to a plan/task address, retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and remove it from `AGENTS.md` required reading, delete the layer-0 duplicate, and only then sweep the prose, which by that point has nothing regenerating it. Recorded as a hypothesis for grooming to validate, not as a requirement.\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-22T13:45:05.957373Z</sub>\\n\\nFull inventory, 2026-08-22. Counts are case-insensitive \\\"task file\\\" occurrences unless stated. Not every occurrence is wrong \u2014 see the exclusions before scoping.\\n\\nLEGITIMATE, DO NOT CHANGE. `sam_schema` contains a genuinely file-based backend, and its file vocabulary is correct: `core/backends/local_yaml.py`, `writers/yaml_writer.py` (12), `readers/detect.py` (7), `readers/yaml_reader.py` (4), `readers/frontmatter_reader.py` (3), `readers/manifest_reader.py` (1), and their tests under `tests_sam/` (test_yaml_writer 9, test_detect 7, test_writers_new 5, test_frontmatter_reader 5, test_query 3, test_normalize 2, test_cli_update 1). Also `scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` (14) and its test (4), which migrate away from files by definition. Anything describing the local YAML backend is accurate about that backend.\\n\\nGENERATED, EXCLUDE FROM ANY SWEEP. `graphify-out/` (GRAPH_REPORT.md 7, graph.json, .graphify_labels.json, four AST cache files) and `docs/workflow-layers/L1-trace-feature-skills.json` \u2014 regenerated artifacts, not sources.\\n\\nSTRUCTURAL CARRIERS \u2014 the identifiers that regenerate the prose. `task_file_path` is a field in production source, not only tests:\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/local_context_backend.py`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/github_context_backend.py`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/memory_context_backend.py`\\n- `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py`\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py`\\n- `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` (documents it as a parameter)\\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`\\n- tests pinning it: `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`, `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`, `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`, `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`\\n- `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` asserts its ABSENCE for one module \u2014 the stalled partial migration\\n\\nCANONICAL DOCUMENTS teaching the model. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (in `AGENTS.md` Required Reading, referenced from ten documents) and its duplicate `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`.\\n\\nAGENT-FACING PROSE, the sweep target. Markdown, highest first:\\n\\ncontext-refinement.md 13, skills/execution/SKILL.md 12, dh-context-gathering.md 9, implementation-manager/SKILL.md 8, skills/dispatch/SKILL.md 6, swarm-task-planner.md 6, AGENTS.md 6, task-decomposition/SKILL.md 5, README.md 5, clear-cove-task-design/SKILL.md 4, start-task/SKILL.md 3, interop/SKILL.md 3, workflow-architecture-diagram.md 3, feature-verifier.md 3, forensic-review/SKILL.md 2, backlog/references/item-schema.md 2, backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md 2, plan-validator.md 2, integration-checker.md 2, code-reviewer.md 2, and one each in work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/interactive-browser.md, generate-task/SKILL.md, final-verification/SKILL.md, dh-meta-docs/SKILL.md, development-harness/references/{language-manifest-schema,default-development-flow,artifact-conventions}.md, docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md, docs/sdlc-layers/layer-1/layer-1-overview.md, docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/README.md, docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md, docs/complexity-fit-and-economics-of-agents.md, docs/backlog-lifecycle.draft.md, docs/backend-providers.md, t0-baseline-capture.md, CONTEXT.md.\\n\\nNote that `AGENTS.md`, `README.md` and `CONTEXT.md` \u2014 the three files an agent or maintainer reads first \u2014 are themselves carriers.\\n\\nDistinct failure kinds inside the prose set, which need different fixes:\\n\\n- Instructs a file operation: `skills/execution/SKILL.md` step \\\"Read Task File\\\"; `implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \\\"extract task file path and task ID\\\".\\n- Names a path in a schema: `backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines `plan` as \\\"relative path to SAM task file\\\".\\n- Right operation, wrong noun: `agents/code-reviewer.md` \\\"Read the SAM task file using `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\\\".\\n- Naming only: \\\"TASK files\\\" as a noun in task-decomposition, final-verification, clear-cove-task-design descriptions.\\n\\nDuplicate check performed before filing: `backlog_list` search across \\\"task file\\\", \\\"task_file_path\\\", \\\"TASK_FILE_FORMAT\\\" returned 155 items, none covering this. Nearest adjacent is #1089 (semantic compaction for completed SAM tasks), which describes task bodies in plan files but is about context size, not the storage model.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **file-based language for sam tasks persists because the context-file key and agents.md required reading still teach it** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-22, while removing file-path language from start-task\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-22T13:57:24.050570Z</sub>\\n\\nSession observations recorded at creation time. These are raw findings for grooming to verify, classify, and scope \u2014 not a completed impact analysis or root-cause determination. Two earlier entries on this item were filed under the headings `Impact Radius` and `Root Cause`; those are grooming-owned section names and the content under them is creation-stage observation, not groomed output. Read them as evidence, and disregard their headings.\\n\\nCorrection to one observation recorded there: the initial note said `task_file_path` appeared in the test suite. It is in production source \u2014 `sam_schema/core/models.py` and all four context backends \u2014 with tests only pinning it. The later entry has the accurate list.\\n\\nNot verified, and left for grooming: whether removing the field from the shared model is the right fix versus moving it behind the local-YAML backend; which consumers actually dereference the value today; whether the session context payload has other consumers beyond the two implementation-manager scripts; and whether the ~92 markdown occurrences split cleanly along the four failure kinds listed, or whether that classification breaks down on inspection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-22T13:47:15.452223Z</sub>\\n\\nCorrecting the Impact Radius section's \\\"legitimate, do not change\\\" carve-out: it was too broad, and the narrowing exposes the actual root.\\n\\nFile storage is one backend behind the `TaskBackend` protocol. File vocabulary is accurate only INSIDE that backend's own implementation, describing what that module does. It is wrong anywhere a task is named as a file, because a task is a backend record and only one backend happens to persist it as YAML.\\n\\nThe leak is in the shared model. `sam_schema/core/models.py` carries a required field:\\n\\n    task_file_path: str = Field(description=\\\"Absolute path to the plan YAML file containing this task.\\\")\\n\\nThat is the domain layer asserting, for every task in every backend, that it has an absolute path to a YAML file.\\n\\nThe backends with no files fabricate one to satisfy it:\\n\\n    memory_context_backend.py:59   task_file_path=f\\\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\\\"\\n    github_context_backend.py:181  task_file_path=_resolve_task_file_path(plan, plan_dir)\\n\\nwith the GitHub helper documented as mirroring `LocalContextBackend._resolve_task_file_path`. The memory backend invents a YAML path for a record held in memory. The GitHub backend synthesizes one for a record stored as an issue. Neither path resolves to anything; both exist only to conform to the model.\\n\\nSo three of four backends manufacture a meaningless value because the shared model requires it, and the one backend where the field is meaningful is the one whose storage model escaped its own boundary.\\n\\nThis reframes the item. The prose is downstream, and no prose sweep can hold while the domain model states that tasks are files \u2014 an agent reading `models.py`, or any generated schema derived from it, is correct to conclude a task has a file path. The same applies to `core/query.py`, which reasons about directory layout at the protocol layer rather than inside a backend.\\n\\nRevised scope, structural first:\\n\\n1. Remove `task_file_path` from the shared model, or move it behind the local-YAML backend where it is true. Delete the fabricating helpers in the memory and GitHub context backends. The stalled assertion in `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` \u2014 which already enforces the field's absence for one module \u2014 is the existing precedent for where this was heading.\\n2. Retire `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, remove it from `AGENTS.md` Required Reading, delete the layer-0 duplicate.\\n3. Then sweep the prose, which by then has nothing regenerating it.\\n\\nSteps 1 and 2 are what make step 3 hold. Doing step 3 alone is what has been tried repeatedly.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-22T13:51:52.497871Z</sub>\\n\\nWhy the field cannot be renamed or made optional \u2014 it is a category error, not a naming problem.\\n\\nA task already has an identity: its address, `P{id}/T{id}`. That address is what every caller passes, what `sam_task` and `sam_plan` resolve, and what the backend uses to return the record.\\n\\n`task_file_path` is not an identity. It is a LOCATION, and location is the backend's private business. The `TaskBackend` protocol exists precisely so the storage form can vary \u2014 a task may be a row in a database, a section inside a Linear plan, a GitHub issue body, an in-memory object, or a YAML file. Only the last of those has a path.\\n\\nSo putting an absolute YAML path in the shared model means the protocol never abstracted storage at all; it required three backends to impersonate the fourth. The fabricated values are the visible cost:\\n\\n    memory_context_backend.py:59   task_file_path=f\\\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\\\"\\n    github_context_backend.py:350  _resolve_task_file_path(...)  # \\\"Mirrors LocalContextBackend._resolve_task_file_path\\\"\\n\\nA record held in memory has no `.yaml`. A GitHub issue has no path resolution. Both synthesize a string that resolves to nothing and that no consumer can dereference.\\n\\nThis settles what the fix is. The field is not renamed to something backend-neutral and not made optional \u2014 it is removed from the shared model, because the information it carries either already exists as the task address or belongs inside the one backend where a path is real. Any consumer currently reading `task_file_path` should be reading the address instead.\\n\\nAcceptance criteria this yields, all observable:\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` declares no path field for a task.\\n- No backend constructs, resolves, or defaults a path in order to satisfy a shared model field. Specifically, `memory_context_backend.py` and `github_context_backend.py` contain no path synthesis, and `_resolve_task_file_path` and its GitHub mirror are gone.\\n- The session context payload written by `dh:start-task` identifies its task by address, not by path. Its consumers \u2014 `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` and `implementation_manager.py` \u2014 read the address.\\n- A test asserts a non-file backend never produces a path, generalising the single-module assertion already in `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py`.\\n- `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` documents an address parameter rather than `task_file_path`.\\n- `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines `plan` as a plan address, not a relative path.\\n\\nThe prose sweep is verifiable only after these hold: at that point `grep -ri \\\"task file\\\"` over agent-facing markdown should return nothing outside the local-YAML backend's own implementation and its tests.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8795d69333a4c1e825c5536ac57ce72fc46095dddb1d48ac6f818fb89fee912d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQLgjsg\"}"}